{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChTsvpcR9TqcKk1JU3zy3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xw52ZuPEwgikqBHbNJhMxK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"printf '%s\\n' 'decision: changes-requested' '```pose-draft' '{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",' '\"findings\":[' '{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":104,\"summary\":\"Regression from the N7 fix: with the root below the repository top, --relative also drops every change outside the root. A changed file at the top gives changed=[] and an empty selection with no error, in worktree and range mode, where the base engine selected the root and non-self-contained modules as a root-level change (reproduced against both versions of validate_scope.go). This narrows validation, against the stated widen-on-uncertainty rule, and no requirement or decision covers it. Reach: the shipped CLI resolves its root to the repository top (cli.go:440) and carry is off below it (by reading), so it affects callers that pass a lower root, the same reach as R1.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\"line\":251,\"summary\":\"carryExclusions still lists top-relative names (no --relative) while the selection is now root-relative, so below the top administrative records are not excluded and widen the selection (seen in a direct probe). workingFileDiffersFromHead and scopeMetadataAt also use `show <head>:<path>`, resolved from the top. Latent and on the safe side: by reading, carry is refused below the top because root/.git is absent.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_index_residuals_test.go\",\"line\":130,\"summary\":\"Text left behind by D1: R3 and R5 still name a report note bound that no longer exists, the len(files[0])>700 assertion cannot fail for a fixed note, the test comment and message still speak of a bounded note, and report.go:313-316 still describes a bounded, redacted line.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_index_residuals_test.go\",\"line\":133,\"summary\":\"By reading: no test fails if the standard-error warning drops Git message, the second clause of R2. This test checks only the warning prefix, and TestTheReportStatesNoPath checks the returned error, not what is printed.\"}' '],' '\"prior_findings\":[' '{\"id\":\"R1-N1\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"check.go reads HEAD:./<path>; TestReadyTransitionsSeeSpecsBelowTheRepositoryTop passes at head and fails with the round 1 check.go overlaid (a spec already in progress is taken for a new transition).\"},' '{\"id\":\"R1-N2\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"reportRedactPaths is removed; report.go reportNote returns a fixed localized string, so no path tail reaches the report; TestTheReportStatesNoPath passes.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R1-N3\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"No substring replacement remains (report.go diff 108f8d27..a73f371a); the versioned report quotes no message, and the warning prints it unaltered.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R1-N4\",\"status\":\"superseded\",\"evidence\":\"Decision D1 rewrites R2: the report states no Git message, so there is no redaction to be incomplete; TestTheReportStatesNoPath passes with a spaced directory name.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R1-N5\",\"status\":\"superseded\",\"evidence\":\"The known-directory replacement and its filepath.Clean were removed from report.go (D1).\"},' '{\"id\":\"R1-N6\",\"status\":\"superseded\",\"evidence\":\"reportAbsolutePathRE and its leading-colon case were removed (D1).\"},' '{\"id\":\"R1-N7\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"Changes under the root are now root-relative (the test passes, and fails with the round 1 validate_scope.go overlaid), but the same flag drops changes outside the root; see N1.\"}' '],' '\"sweep\":\"The nine code files of the range, with the round 2 delta read line by line: check.go ready transitions, report.go note and warning, validate_scope.go and its consumers in validate.go and validate_carry.go, CLI root resolution, the amended spec with D1, the changed tests; focused tests and go vet, base and previous-round overlays, a probe of changes outside a lower root, and every planned pose tool including both validate runs.\",' '\"criteria\":[' '{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\",\"rationale\":\"The assumption that --relative only renames paths is false: it also filters to the root. D1 premise that free text paths have no delimiter holds; L1 was read and is not disputed.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"No new shared production state; the concurrent index-read test passed in the focused run; L1 covers the ledger deadline.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"No schema or tool contract changes; the new report line and the scope failure are stated in the spec API section. The selection answer is covered by N1.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"A failed untracked listing fails selection with a bounded cause; the report note is fixed text.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The warning on standard error still formats the whole error; the versioned report points to it. Its test gap is N4.\"},' '{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\",\"rationale\":\"At the repository top nothing differs; below it, selection answers differently for outside changes.\"},' '{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},' '{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\",\"rationale\":\"HEAD:./ addresses the cause of R1-N1 and D1 removes the cause of the redaction defects. The scope fix addresses naming but also changes which files are listed. The design assessment observed no structural deltas.\"},' '{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Examined the amended spec and the changed-scope text in architecture.md and monorepo-recipes.md: they match behaviour for the CLI, whose root is the repository top. Leftover wording is N3.\"},' '{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The report says the list could not be read and where the cause was printed; the warning and the selection error carry Git words.\"},' '{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"R1 to R5 as amended each have a passing focused test; the gaps in R2 and R5 evidence are low and listed as N3 and N4.\"},' '{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},' '{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The versioned report now interpolates nothing from Git, so no checkout path can enter it through this note; revisions stay validated before reaching Git.\"},' '{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Dropping the message is smaller than redaction and meets amended R2; it would need revisiting if the report had to carry the cause. HEAD:./ is a minimal fix.\"}' '],' '\"tools\":[' '{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\"