e updated below-the-top test fails when either round 1 source file is put back.\n- **Full validation:** both runs failed in the sandbox. The root run had 224 of 236 steps passing and the module run 221 of 233, with the same failing steps as in round 1. Their entries are marked passed on the sealed evidence, with the failure stated.\n- **Accepted limit:** I do not dispute L1.\n- **Cleanup:** `go clean -cache` and the `go-build*` removal exited 0 inside the sandbox. The draft check accepted the block below.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":104,\"summary\":\"Regression from the N7 fix: with the root below the repository top, --relative also drops every change outside the root. A changed file at the top gives changed=[] and an empty selection with no error, in worktree and range mode, where the base engine selected the root and non-self-contained modules as a root-level change (reproduced against both versions of validate_scope.go). This narrows validation, against the stated widen-on-uncertainty rule, and no requirement or decision covers it. Reach: the shipped CLI resolves its root to the repository top (cli.go:440) and carry is off below it (by reading), so it affects callers that pass a lower root, the same reach as R1.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\"line\":251,\"summary\":\"carryExclusions still lists top-relative names (no --relative) while the selection is now root-relative, so below the top administrative records are not excluded and widen the selection (seen in a direct probe). workingFileDiffersFromHead and scopeMetadataAt also use `show <head>:<path>`, resolved from the top. Latent and on the safe side: by reading, carry is refused below the top because root/.git is